From eed23bb5432b9b3247933bf34252d49c53d4885f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Reed <reedswork@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] websocket: flush every frame written

fastwebsockets writes a frame into the stream without flushing it, and a
wisp stream's AsyncWrite only hands the packet to the transport sink,
which sends it on its next poll: the socket's next frame, or a write of
another stream on the same wisp connection. A message the page sent, the
page's close, and the answers to the server's ping and close waited in
epoxy until then, so a server answering the page looked silent until the
page wrote again, and a close the server started was not answered.
send, close and the read loop's obligated sends now flush the frame.
